WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:02.385
Lesson 7.6.

00:00:02.385 --> 00:00:03.925
Network activity.

00:00:03.925 --> 00:00:06.382
By the end of this lesson, you'll be able

00:00:06.382 --> 00:00:09.659
to judge a chain's real usage beyond transaction counts.

00:00:10.959 --> 00:00:12.249
Here's the plan.

00:00:12.249 --> 00:00:13.934
First, the key ideas.

00:00:13.934 --> 00:00:16.649
Then, a worked example, step by step.

00:00:16.649 --> 00:00:18.174
Then, your checklist.

00:00:18.174 --> 00:00:20.336
And finally, a three-question quiz.

00:00:21.636 --> 00:00:25.115
Transaction counts depend on architecture and bots.

00:00:25.115 --> 00:00:28.360
Better: fees paid (real demand for blockspace),

00:00:28.360 --> 00:00:31.740
stablecoin activity, DEX volume, app revenue, and

00:00:31.740 --> 00:00:33.700
retention of users over time.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:37.515
Let's work an example, step by step.

00:00:37.515 --> 00:00:41.825
Chain A: 5M transactions/day, $20k fees.

00:00:41.825 --> 00:00:46.387
Chain B: 500k transactions/day, $2M fees.

00:00:46.387 --> 00:00:49.397
B's users pay 100× more for blockspace,

00:00:49.397 --> 00:00:52.182
a stronger sign of valuable activity.

00:00:53.481 --> 00:00:54.941
Here's your checklist.

00:00:54.941 --> 00:00:56.476
Do it now, for real.

00:00:56.476 --> 00:00:58.162
First, Fees and app revenue

00:00:58.162 --> 00:01:00.751
compared, not just transaction counts.

00:01:00.751 --> 00:01:03.046
And finally, Bot activity considered.

00:01:04.346 --> 00:01:05.556
Question 1.

00:01:05.556 --> 00:01:06.851
Why are fees a better

00:01:06.851 --> 00:01:09.028
usage signal than transaction counts?

00:01:13.448 --> 00:01:15.698
The answer: Paying fees shows real

00:01:15.698 --> 00:01:17.948
demand; counts are easy to inflate.

00:01:19.249 --> 00:01:20.494
Question 2.

00:01:20.494 --> 00:01:22.249
What distorts transaction counts?

00:01:26.669 --> 00:01:29.334
The answer: Bots, batching and chain design.

00:01:30.634 --> 00:01:31.904
Question 3.

00:01:31.904 --> 00:01:33.829
Name one strong activity metric.

00:01:38.129 --> 00:01:40.290
The answer: Fees, app revenue,

00:01:40.290 --> 00:01:42.939
stablecoin activity or user retention.

00:01:44.239 --> 00:01:46.754
Do the checklist now, before you move on.

00:01:46.754 --> 00:01:50.849
Next up, Lesson 7.7: DEX & liquidity analytics.
